{
	"name": "Blessings and Curses",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/skills/social/trading-justice-scale-gold.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>At 1st level, a hedge wizard can inflict benefits and penalties upon their targets. Your hedge wizard may use this ability a number of times equal to your proficiency modifier per long rest, and the target must be within 30ft.</p><p><strong>Blessing.</strong> When your hedge wizard applies a blessing, the target gains a 1d4 expertise die they can use on an attack roll or saving throw within the next minute. Applying a blessing is a bonus action.</p><p><strong>Curse.</strong> When your hedge wizard applies a curse, the target takes a 1d4 penalty on an attack roll or saving throw. Using this ability is a reaction to the target making an attack roll or saving throw.</p>",
